  "summary": "A Japanese street fashion tribe known for colorful, layered outfits and eccentric accessories, originating in Harajuku.",
  "description": "Takenoku Zoku (竹の子族, \"bamboo shoot tribe\") was a Japanese street fashion tribe that emerged in Harajuku in the late 1970s and early 1980s. Known for colorful, layered outfits and eccentric accessories, they were among the first Japanese youth subcultures to develop a distinctive visual style independent of Western fashion. The tribe was named for their bamboo shoot-like growth in the Harajuku area.",
